    "manifestation": "hang",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "Calling QR decomposition on a symbolic matrix whose rank handling is problematic (rank-deficient due to symbolic linear dependence)",
      "Example constructs a 5x5 matrix M with entries linear in x, then sets M[4,:] = M[1,:] + M[2,:], after which M.QRdecomposition() hangs and is interrupted with ^C / KeyboardInterrupt"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "In [28]: M = randMatrix(5)*x + randMatrix(5)\nIn [29]: M[4,:] = M[1,:] + M[2,:]",
        "buggy_output": "In [31]: M.QRdecomposition()\nKeyboardInterrupt (operation did not finish)",
        "expected_output": null,
        "value_kind": "exception",
        "source": "discussion:PR#29040 (example shows M.QRdecomposition() followed by ^C and KeyboardInterrupt)"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": [
      "Release notes: \"Fix how QR decomposition handles rank of matrix with symbols\"",
      "Code change in sympy/matrices/decompositions.py adds checks based on z = Q[:, i].is_zero_matrix and norm = dps(dot(Q[:, i], Q[:, i])) and special-cases when z is None and norm.equals(0), to avoid problematic zero checking for symbolic expressions"
    ]
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": null,
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": null,
    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Test added: for symbolic dependent columns A = Matrix([[a, k*a],[b, k*b]]) with symbols a,b,k (real=True), QRdecomposition should respect that rank(A)=1 and Q has exactly A.rank() columns.",
      "For the same A, the test asserts Q*R reconstructs A exactly up to simplification: (Q*R - A).applyfunc(simplify) == zeros(2, 2).",
      "The test also asserts the orthonormality/normalization does not produce invalid entries: QQ = (Q.H * Q).applyfunc(simplify) and assert not QQ.has(S.NaN)."
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "Reproduction may be sensitive to symbolic assumptions (a,b,k created with real=True) because correctness relies on rank/zero detection for symbolic expressions.",
      "Any reproduction depending on numerical thresholds is not evidenced here; using floats or different simplification/equality checks could change whether the failure is observed.",
      "The core change involves using dps(dot(Q[:, i], Q[:, i])) and equality-to-zero logic; reproductions that differ in dps precision or equality simplification strategy may not hit the same path."
    ]
  },
